# Claude Code's own scratch, which it writes INSIDE the repo — none of it authored here.
#
# The worktrees are what forced this: a review agent given `isolation: worktree` gets a whole
# checkout at `.claude/worktrees/`, and every path above is repo-root-relative so none of them match
# the copy. Measured — ONE live worktree turns `format:check` red on 716 files of vendored Codex
# protocol types, and 115 had three at once, which is exactly the 2,148 it reported.
#
# ⚠️ Scoped to the whole directory rather than to `worktrees/`, and that is a correction: the
# narrower version claimed the rest of `.claude/` was real repo content, and `git ls-files .claude`
# returns ZERO. Everything in there is harness state — `settings.local.json` and
# `scheduled_tasks.lock` today, and `skills/**/SKILL.md` or `agents/*.md` the moment either is
# installed, which are markdown and which prettier does reflow. That is a red gate on a file nobody
# in this repo wrote and nobody here can fix: the same blocker as the worktrees, one level up.
# ⚑ No trailing-path separator, so it matches a `.claude/` at any depth, not only the root one.
.claude/

